 ## Overview
 Viewpoint Preference Analysis quantifies expert preferences in volume rendering by analyzing a database of existing rendered images [S1]. It recovers camera viewpoints from these images using category-specific Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) and accumulates the resulting probability distributions to generate a viewing map [S1]. Unlike methods that optimize transfer functions or lighting parameters, this approach operates on the geometric configuration of the camera to identify regions of high expert consensus, such as side views for fish or front views for vessels [S1].
